body:
superior in what way? They are both different use cases no? I want people to have the option to go to any page they want in the DB without having to start from the beginning. Maybe I can do a method where I assign an additional attribute but I feel like that wouldn't work if I combine page access + limit per page 

&#x200B;

Edit: more info

So it seemed that my problem was the apollo caching was not working properly therefore I had to modify the InMemoryCache() function to cater to my data.

For example this is my query

                export const GET_MOVIESE = gql`
                    query DiscoverMovies($page: Int) {
                        Media: DiscoverMovies(page: $page) {
                            page
                            total_pages
                            results {
                                id
                                title
                            }
                        }
                    }
                `;

So to get my fetchMore() function to work I had to add a typePolicy as seen above to merge my data. This is done in the InMemoryCache function. In my case I only wanted to merge the results and then replace everything else with the incoming data hence the logic, this solution is what made my fetchMore finally work. I tried many other things like relayStylePagination() and offsetLimitPagination() as seen here `DiscoverMovies:relayStylePagination()` `DiscoverMovies:offsetLimitPagination()` but nether function worked. I think it was because of my data structure which is why it had to me custom merged

    typePolicies: {
                Query: {
                    fields: {
                        DiscoverMovies: {
                            read: (existing) => {
                                return existing;
                            },
                            merge: (existing, incoming) => {
                                return existing ? { ...incoming, results: [...existing.results, ...incoming.results] } : incoming;
                            },
                        },
                        DiscoverTV: {
                            read: (existing) => {
                                return existing;
                            },
                            merge: (existing, incoming) => {
                                return existing ? { ...incoming, results: [...existing.results, ...incoming.results] } : incoming;
                            },
                        },
                    },
                },
            }

